values ('bbbb0002-0000-4000-8000-00000000001f', 'en', null, 'Machine Learning: Learning From Data', 'The mathematical theory of learning from data: when a rule fit on a finite sample will actually generalize to unseen cases, and how model complexity, the bias-variance tradeoff, regularization, and validation all bear on that one question. Structure adapted from Caltech''s open ''Learning From Data'' course (work.caltech.edu); all explanations original.', null, 'career', 31, true, 'technology', '{bbbb0001-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b}')
